---

Pick a binding to use glowcap from your language. Each one exposes the same
operations over the C ABI. The Rust, Python, TypeScript, and Racket bindings
load the Host and the driver loop, then add transport archives as needed. The
browser package runs the Host as WebAssembly. [Choose an API]($link.page('surfaces'))
compares these bindings with the Zig package, C ABI, CLI, and browser package,
and [Concepts]($link.page('concepts')) explains the capability model behind
them.

[Every binding wraps the same C ABI, so the session operations and transport choices are the same in each language.]($image.siteAsset('diagram-bindings.svg'))

# One contract, each language's idioms

A `Session` gives you the verbs in the
[bindings contract](https://github.com/jimisaacs/glowcap/blob/main/bindings/README.md).
A `Host` manages many sessions and the introductions between them
([modules]($link.page('modules'))). A `Ref` is a capability in hand: pass it as
an argument and the access moves with it.

| Binding | Entry point | Async idiom | Actor idiom |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| [Rust]($link.page('bindings/rust')) | `Runtime`, `Session`, typed enums | tokio (opt-in `async`) | `spawn` over closures |
| [TypeScript]($link.page('bindings/ts')) | `Runtime`, `Session` class | JavaScript promises | `spawn` over callbacks |
| [Python]($link.page('bindings/python')) | `Runtime`, `Session`, Python values | `asyncio` | `spawn` over callables |
| [Racket]($link.page('bindings/racket')) | `Runtime`, `session`, event structs | green threads + ports | Goblins-faithful |

`Runtime.open(...)` installs transports once. `runtime.connect(locator)`
returns a session whose handshake is complete.

In the browser, `@glowcap/web` compiles the same `Session` API to WebAssembly.
A browser dials but never listens. See
[In the browser]($link.page('bindings/browser')).

Stay at the level you need: synchronous verbs, the language's own async sockets,
or the Goblins-shaped actor layer on top with near-call and eventual-send
([modules]($link.page('modules'))).

# Use a binding from a checkout

The packages and archives live in a glowcap checkout. Pin a commit, run
`zig build`, and use the binding in that tree. Set `GLOWCAP_LIB_DIR` to load the
archives from another directory. The
[packaging notes](https://github.com/jimisaacs/glowcap/blob/main/bindings/PACKAGING.md)
give the full search order.

The [binding README](https://github.com/jimisaacs/glowcap/blob/main/bindings/README.md)
has the path for each language. Compose
[iroh]($link.page('transports/iroh')),
[onion]($link.page('transports/onion')),
[Noise]($link.page('transports/noise')), or
[WebRTC]($link.page('transports/webrtc'))
from their archives. The TCP archive carries Noise over TCP, plus the `tcp`
and `inproc` transports used for testing.
